          "type": "text",
          "text": "I can’t see your account/billing settings from here, so I can’t confirm your plan directly. In the Git/CLI version of Amp, “free vs paid” switching is usually controlled in your Amp account on the web, not inside the local repo.\n\nFor the pixelated look, that’s usually display/rendering (not plan-related). Quick things to try on Windows:\n\n1. Check terminal font and disable bitmap-like fonts (`Settings -> Profiles -> Appearance -> Font face` in Windows Terminal).\n2. Set Windows display scaling to a common value like `100%` or `125%`, then restart terminal.\n3. Disable GPU text rendering in the terminal (toggle hardware acceleration off/on, depending on terminal).\n4. If using tmux/SSH, make sure you’re not in a low-color mode (`TERM` should usually be `xterm-256color`).\n\nIf you want, I can walk you through exact steps for your setup (Windows Terminal vs VS Code terminal vs Git Bash) and help make it crisp."
        }
